findings.proposal:
Add `?cloudShadowEvery=N` (proposed 2; 1 = today, byte-identical).

In cloud_volume.js after effect creation, wrap the instance methods. No vendor edit needed:
```js
const sm = effect.shadowMaps, sp = effect.shadowPass;
const smU = sm.update.bind(sm), spU = sp.update.bind(sp);
let n = 0, own = 0;
sm.update = (...a) => { if (n % N === 0) smU(...a); };
sp.update = (r, f, dt) => { if (n % N === 0) spU(r, ++own, dt); n++; };
```
- Cascades and the shadow buffer stay frozen together on skipped frames, so clouds, AP shafts and terrain all sample a consistent pair.
- Passing `++own` instead of the effect frame keeps consecutive STBN slices per run, avoiding the 64-frame cycling cloud_volume.js:169-174 fought.
- Force a run on cascade-count/mapSize change and after a teleport.

findings.evidence:
Split chain (default at high/ultra: particlesOverCloudsEnabled true when absent, particles_over_clouds.js:54-62; cloudsMainPass on). Pass order:
- an own `EffectPass(camera, scrub)` (atmosphere_pipeline.js:1924-1927);
- ssao;
- `fxPass = new PostChainSourcePass(camera, null, ...atmosEffects)` writing the composer buffer (1865);
- `lateHazePass = new PostChainHazePass(layeredHaze, …)` reading it and writing T (1866; layered_haze.js:144-165 renders a full-screen quad);
- late particles, late scrub, fxPostPass.

The scrub's own comment (1806-1812) says it must be a separate pass only because bloom blurs its raw input. On the split chain bloom sits in fxPostPass behind the late scrub (1870-1872). Nothing between scrub #1 and fxPass reads colour: ssaoPass reads depth only, and the atmos effects (fxDistort, ssaoComposite, fxDecals, clouds, AP) read only inputColor, depth or their own buffers.

LAYER_HAZE_FRAG (layered_haze.js:60-91) is purely per-pixel (colour, depth, uniforms). `PostChainTargetPass` (515-530) already renders the atmos effects straight into T; it is the haze-off path at 1868.

Each removed pass is a full-screen RGBA16F read plus write (and a depth read for the haze) at drawing-buffer resolution, plus a renderer.render call on the main thread and on CrGpuMain.

findings.proposal:
In _finalizeInstBuckets and SharedAlphaBuckets.finalize, when b.n > 0:
```
im.instanceMatrix.clearUpdateRanges(); im.instanceMatrix.addUpdateRange(0, b.n*16);
im.instanceColor.clearUpdateRanges(); im.instanceColor.addUpdateRange(0, b.n*im.instanceColor.itemSize);
```
Buffer creation stays a full upload, since three's createBuffer uses bufferData on the whole array; clear the ranges anyway. Optionally also `setUsage(DynamicDrawUsage)` at bucket creation and in _growBucket. Escape flag `?particleUploadRange=off`. The draw count is already n, so the instances drawn are byte-identical.

Keep a `_newSources` set filled by bindEmitterFxLight. At the top of tickFxLights, for each new source:
- resolve its position once;
- set `registered = d² < REGISTER_RADIUS²`;
- set `suppressed` by testing it against the current kept and registered set and the static positions cached from the last dedupe (O(new × kept));
- then clear the set.

The full dedupe stays at 2 Hz. The light pool size is unchanged (sources only compete for the fixed 16+2 slots), so there is no program relink, per wall 110. Escape flag `?fxLightInstantReg=off`.

