verdicts.code_truth:
The code facts are accurate.
- DEFAULT_HZ = 30 (vitals-orbs.js:155).
- createDriver tick (:961-966) writes back/body/clip and the meniscus `d` attributes per vessel per tick, and mutates .wsurf via surfXform.setTranslate (:975-976). getAnimations() (orbAnimSync.step) forces a style flush per tick (:860-900, comment :911-913).
- Stylesheet:
  - .subglow blur(6px) + screen (:634);
  - .lqwall multiply (:637), clipped to the live wave (SVG :421 clip-path lqc);
  - .sspec blur(2.6px) + screen + an infinite transform animation (:638-645);
  - .caustics screen, clipped to the live wave (:646, SVG :394);
  - .bub animated (:655);
  - .shimmer blur(6px) animated (:662-666).
- subglow and sspec sit inside .wsurf (:423-425), so they move every tick.
- The url-flags rows (:685-688) record the v1/v2 raster ablations the finder cites.

The claim that multiply forces a Skia destination copy on ANGLE D3D11 is plausible (multiply is not a coefficient blend mode, and ANGLE D3D11 has no advanced blend). It is not verified here and cannot be without a GPU trace.

verdicts.corrected_claim:
three r184's A2C variant could anti-alias the hard per-pixel cutout edges of opaque pure-ClipMap materials on the MSAA world target, at default msaa=2 into about 3 coverage levels, at roughly zero fps cost.

It does not reproduce retail's blended edge: edge RGB stays darkened unless visuals-1's dilation also lands.

It needs:
- an alpha=1 guarantee at the canvas (a final-pass alpha write, or visuals-3);
- A2C variants added to shader prewarm;
- fade owners clearing and restoring alphaToCoverage;
- replication in static_atlas and static_array_pool without key changes;
- a 1070 eye test (msaa 2 vs 4, NVIDIA dither).
